 "audition": [
  "album 0.62-6.0 s (with a4-30-01 under it): the STRAIGHT violin, senza vibrato -- sincere, plain, never \"world's smallest violin\"; the dead stop at 6.0 s (the lock's first heart) should get the laugh",
  "album 24.38-31.88 s: Tasya's floor -- ironic beauty (the landlord's chord); the Rhodes on the beats only; nothing moves under \"hi.\" / \"Hello.\"; the home chord at 30.62 s is the landlord's last word, cut on the boardroom",
  "album 33.75-47.5 s: LEVERAGE low under Terb, running through the freeze card; the thud is a pitched thud, never an 808 kit or a heartbeat; the drop-out on \"Terms?\" (47.5 s) IS the move. Fix 2b: the cello pizz notched at 110.5 Hz and the F pedal re-bowed at 39.38 and 44.38 s: does it sound minor, still woody, and is the bow change inaudible?",
  "album 63.12 s and 68.75 s: the Build restarting reads as joy (Gerg is back), and the pickup lands with the sand into the sign",
  "album 69.38 s: the ONE stab -- earned, one size too big for a lobby sign -- then the cut to one chip note at 71.88 s undercuts it",
  "album 73.75-80.88 s: F F F (1-bit, uneven), the bonk slot, silence, then the felt C4 -> F4 after \"okay.\" ringing into the Q* hum -- the right last word, or one too many?"
 ],
